      "text": "It is said to make its home somewhere in the sea. It guides crews of shipwrecks to shore.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dragonite is capable of circling the globe in just 16 hours. It is a kindhearted Pokémon that leads lost and foundering ships in a storm to the safety of land.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dragonite is capable of circling the globe in just 16 hours. It is a kindhearted Pokémon that leads lost and foundering ships in a storm to the safety of land.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon saved a shipwrecked man, taking him to a remote island—a paradise occupied solely by Dragonite.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Incur the wrath of this normally calm Pokémon at your peril, because it will smash everything to smithereens before it’s satisfied.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It flies over raging seas as if they were nothing. Observing this, a ship’s captain dubbed this Pokémon “the sea incarnate.”",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "You’ll often hear tales of this kindhearted Pokémon rescuing people or Pokémon that are drowning.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is said that this Pokémon lives somewhere in the sea and that it flies. However, these are only rumors.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is said that this Pokémon lives somewhere in the sea and that it flies. However, these are only rumors.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s a kindhearted Pokémon. If it spots a drowning person or Pokémon, Dragonite simply must help them.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon is known as the Sea Incarnate. Figureheads that resemble Dragonite decorate the bows of many ships.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
